<title>USA: USDA's Glickman -- monitoring Canada wheat exports.</title>
<headline>USDA's Glickman -- monitoring Canada wheat exports.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman said Tuesday the department was monitoring Canadina wheat exports and said it would not tolerate market disruptions.</p>
<p>&quot;We are monitoring it. We will not tolerate market disruptions from imports of Canadian grain,&quot; Glickman told the House Agriculture Committee.  </p>
<p>At the hearing, Glickman was asked about high levels of spring wheat and durum wheat exports to the United States from Canada and whether the United States would act if they exceeded limits agreed to in 1994.</p>
<p>Glickman told the House panel, &quot;we are concerned about it. We will take action if we think there is a market disruption.&quot;</p>
</text>
